    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38164" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-vēlo</span></b> , āre,
			v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to veil</i> or <i>cover over; to
				conceal by placing before</i> (late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flammea praevelatura pudorem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. Rapt. Pros. 2, 325</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praevelans fronde secures,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. VI. Cons. Honor. 647</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amnem Tiberis domibus amoenis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Laud. Stil. 2, 189</span></i>
			. </div>
